    </header>
    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="7" relname="span">It seems like there is a consistency domain amongst many applications.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="3" relname="concession">For example, in the Microsoft Office Suite the floppy disk icon means the same thing in all of the applications;</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="8" relname="span">however as one moves into the more specialized elements of the applications the consistency domain is within that given application not between the applications.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="9" relname="span">A floppy disk icon can be seen in many applications from different vendors like Adobe Acrobate Reader</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="4" relname="elaboration">and in most of them they mean "save".</segment>
        <group id="6" type="span"/>
        <group id="7" type="span" parent="6" relname="span"/>
        <group id="8" type="span" parent="1" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="9" type="span" parent="7" relname="elaboration"/>
    </body>
</rst>
